---
import '@/styles/global.css';
import ThemeProvider from '@/components/ThemeProvider.astro';
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro';
import ComputationalMedicineBrief from '@/components/ComputationalMedicineBrief.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>A Computational View of Medicine | Eir Open</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A white paper by Birger Moëll, Erica Hughberg, and Maria Undén Morein on why AI matters most where disease becomes a patient-specific search problem."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <ThemeProvider />
    <SiteHeader current="docs" />
    <main class="page-shell">
      <section class="hero-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">White Paper</p>
        <h1>A Computational View of Medicine</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Why AI will matter most where disease becomes a search problem.
        </p>
        <div class="meta-row">
          <span>Birger Moëll, Erica Hughberg, and Maria Undén Morein</span>
          <span>Eir Space</span>
          <span>March 17, 2026</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="primary-link" href="/papers/computational-view-of-medicine.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            Open PDF
          </a>
          <a class="secondary-link" href="/docs/ai-compute-disease-ranking/">View the ranking</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="copy-grid">
        <article class="copy-card">
          <p class="section-kicker">Abstract</p>
          <h2>The core claim</h2>
          <p>
            The paper argues that the most important use of advanced AI in health
            is not generic automation. It is high-context reasoning over disease
            classes where better synthesis can change diagnosis, treatment
            selection, escalation, or trial matching for a specific patient.
          </p>
          <p>
            Precision oncology, rare-disease genomics, resistant infection, and
            sepsis rise to the top because they combine large search spaces with
            fragmented multimodal data and decisions that are highly sensitive
            to patient context.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="copy-card">
          <p class="section-kicker">Why it matters</p>
          <h2>From records to leverage</h2>
          <p>
            Once patients can access and assemble their own records, compute
            becomes part of personal health infrastructure. The paper makes the
            case that data access without reasoning access is incomplete
            empowerment.
          </p>
          <p>
            The operational goal is not “AI doctor in a box.” It is stronger,
            better-prepared patient-clinician reasoning around the cases where
            synthesis is the bottleneck.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="copy-card full-width">
        <p class="section-kicker">Evidence base</p>
        <h2>What the paper uses</h2>
        <ul class="sources-list">
          <li>Personalized RNA cancer vaccines in melanoma</li>
          <li>AlphaFold and protein consequence modeling</li>
          <li>Genome sequencing for rare-disease diagnosis</li>
          <li>Deep learning-guided antibiotic discovery</li>
          <li>TREWS prospective sepsis deployment</li>
          <li>AI-enabled ECG pragmatic randomized trial</li>
          <li>Cluster-randomized deterioration surveillance</li>
          <li>Longitudinal EHR deep learning</li>
          <li>OpenNotes and patient access to records</li>
          <li>Patient use of LLMs on open notes</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <ComputationalMedicineBrief />

      <section class="paper-frame">
        <iframe
          title="A Computational View of Medicine PDF"
          src="/papers/computational-view-of-medicine.pdf#view=FitH"
        />
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(232, 168, 48, 0.12), transparent 28%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--background), var(--background-soft));
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
  }

  .page-shell {
    width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 2rem));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 0 4rem;
  }

  .hero-card,
  .copy-card,
  .paper-frame {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 1.75rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--card) 94%, white 6%);
    box-shadow: var(--card-shadow);
  }

  .hero-card {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 88% 14%, rgba(232, 168, 48, 0.14), transparent 24%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--card) 92%, white 8%), var(--card));
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 12ch;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.7rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  .lede,
  p,
  li {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .meta-row,
  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  .meta-row span,
  .primary-link,
  .secondary-link {
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .meta-row span {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    background: var(--background-soft);
  }

  .primary-link {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
  }

  .secondary-link {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    color: var(--foreground);
  }

  .copy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .copy-card,
  .paper-frame {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1.6rem;
  }

  .sources-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .paper-frame {
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  iframe {
    width: 100%;
    height: min(78vh, 1100px);
    border: 0;
    display: block;
    background: white;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .copy-grid,
    .sources-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero-card {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
